Yes. For Elastic Cloud Hosted (SaaS), there are many responsibilities that are fully owned by Elastic. Below is a detailed list you can directly use in your responsibility matrix.

Task ID	Section	Sub-Section	Task Description	Detailed Activities	Responsibility
1.1	Platform Ops	Cluster Health	Cluster Availability Management	Monitor cluster health, node health, service availability, automatic recovery of failed nodes, maintain cluster uptime.	Elastic
1.2	Platform Ops	Infrastructure	Infrastructure Provisioning	Provision and manage compute instances, storage volumes, networking, and underlying cloud resources.	Elastic
1.3	Platform Ops	Maintenance	Operating System Maintenance	Perform OS patching, security updates, kernel updates, and operating system maintenance on all managed nodes.	Elastic
1.4	Platform Ops	Maintenance	Elasticsearch Version Maintenance	Provide supported Elasticsearch versions, maintain platform compatibility, manage infrastructure required for upgrades. (Customer chooses when to upgrade.)	Elastic
1.5	Platform Ops	Maintenance	Kibana Platform Maintenance	Maintain Kibana infrastructure, availability, patching, and platform health.	Elastic
1.6	Platform Ops	Hardware	Hardware Maintenance	Replace failed hardware, storage devices, compute resources, and underlying infrastructure components without customer involvement.	Elastic
1.7	Platform Ops	High Availability	Automatic Node Recovery	Detect failed nodes and automatically recreate or replace them while maintaining cluster availability.	Elastic
1.8	Platform Ops	Storage	Disk Management	Provision, manage, and replace storage volumes, monitor storage hardware failures, and maintain storage infrastructure.	Elastic
1.9	Platform Ops	Networking	Platform Networking	Maintain internal cluster networking, load balancers, TLS between nodes, DNS, and service connectivity within the managed platform.	Elastic
1.10	Platform Ops	Security	Platform Security	Secure the managed infrastructure, apply platform security patches, vulnerability remediation, and infrastructure hardening.	Elastic
1.11	Platform Ops	Monitoring	Platform Monitoring	Continuously monitor platform components, cluster infrastructure, resource utilization, and perform proactive remediation.	Elastic
1.12	Platform Ops	Disaster Recovery	Infrastructure Recovery	Recover managed infrastructure following hardware or infrastructure failures according to Elastic Cloud SLAs.	Elastic
1.13	Platform Ops	Capacity	Infrastructure Scaling Support	Provide mechanisms for scaling deployments (memory, storage, topology changes) while maintaining platform stability.	Elastic
1.14	Platform Ops	Certificates	Platform Certificate Management	Manage certificates used for Elastic Cloud endpoints and platform communications.	Elastic
1.15	Platform Ops	Support	Platform Incident Management	Investigate and resolve platform-related incidents affecting Elastic Cloud infrastructure and service availability.	Elastic
